ss  this maritime region  that's been the subject of my own book  the so-called belton road the maritime  silk road the extension of influence  through investment and infrastructure  and technology on the one hand that may  be a good thing for local development if  there are infrastructure needs but on  the other hand it's quite clear that the  chinese state is using these methods to  extend its influence  over a wide range of small countries so  that in turn  it can in time project security and  military power it really is a kind of  empire by stealth and the concern for a  country like australia  is that if you like we are being  out flanked in our own  neighborhood in our own region a chinese  military force in the solomon islands  would essentially  block the way between australia and its  ally the united states  rory metcalf we leave it there for the  time being but thank you so much for  joining us today  you
 

